bout colleagues. So reliability, stress resilience, but poor teamwork (nasty remarks) and memory issue.\n\nCandidate C: makes correct decisions quickly, keeps calm in crisis, understands complicated technology. Concerns: difficulty communicating ideas, regarded as egocentric, not willing to further education. So good decision, stress, technical, but poor communication and development.\n\nCandidate D: responds to unexpected events adequately, concentrates well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously. Concerns: regarded as know-it-all, hot temper. So good problem solving, responsibility, but temper and attitude.\n\nWe need best overall fit. Likely candidate D has many strengths, but hot temper is serious for crew cooperation. Candidate B has stress and conscientiousness but nasty remarks are big. Candidate C has calmness and decision but communication issues. Candidate A has leadership but show-off and not open to ideas.\n\nWhich is strongest overall? Maybe D: responsibility, problem solving, concentration, adaptability, but hot temper could affect crew cooperation. However, hot temper may be mitigated? Not sure.\n\nWe could ask other agents for missing info: e.g., does Candidate D's hot temper affect crew cooperation? But we have no further info.\n\nWe need to make a contribution. Since no prior discussion, we can propose a candidate and give reasoning. Choose Candidate D as current recommendation, acknowledging concerns.\n\nLet's produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE: state recommendation for D, reference strengths and concerns, argue why D still best overall despite temper, because strengths cover many criteria.\n\nMETADATA_JSON vote D."}
